<title>CHILE: Endesa confirms Outokumpu deal.</title>
<headline>Endesa confirms Outokumpu deal.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean power giant Empresa Nacional de Electricidad SA (Endesa) confirmed it has signed an deal with Finland's Outokumpu Oy to study building a copper smelter and refinery in the northern Atacama Desert.</p>
<p>&quot;As a first step, both companies will order a technical and economic feasibility study to be presented to financial institutions,&quot; said the statement.</p>
<p>The companies plan to invest $800 million to build a plant which will produce 300,000 tonnes of copper cathodes a year. If it is built, the complex will be one of the third largest in Chile.  </p>
<p>Endesa, Chile's largest power generator, said it has set up a new division to identify potential mining projects.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212</p>
